<div class="security-info">
    <h2>Password Security & Cryptography</h2>

    <p>
        Strong passwords should be long, unique, and contain a mixture of
        uppercase letters, lowercase letters, numbers, and special characters.
    </p>

    <p>
        Passwords should not be stored as plain text. In real applications,
        passwords are protected using secure hashing techniques such as
        bcrypt, Argon2, or scrypt.
    </p>

    <p>
        <strong>Hashing:</strong> A password is converted into a fixed-length
        value that is difficult to reverse. This helps protect passwords if
        a database is compromised.
    </p>

    <p>
        <strong>Important:</strong> Never reuse the same password across
        different websites or applications.
    </p>
</div>